WEBVTT

00:02.102 --> 00:04.036
Come on. Just one more race.

00:04.104 --> 00:06.334
- Every time we race, you lose.
- You always lose.

00:06.406 --> 00:08.397
One more race,
and then we'll go to the strip club.

00:08.475 --> 00:10.466
All right.
Three, two, one.

00:15.782 --> 00:17.750
- Goddamn it!
- What is wrong with you?

00:17.817 --> 00:20.650
- Super slow drinker over here.
- Do you have, like, a little throat or something?

00:20.720 --> 00:22.551
- Dennis. We gotta get out of here now.
- Why?

00:22.622 --> 00:24.817
I just got off the phone with Dad.
He wants to stop by and talk to us.

00:24.891 --> 00:27.519
- What does Dad want?
- I don't know! Let's go before we have to deal with this!

00:27.594 --> 00:30.028
Let's get out of here before
you guys get around your father.

00:30.096 --> 00:33.088
Let's just take care of one more...
Don't... Don't be grabby.

00:33.166 --> 00:36.135
Okay. Dennis,
I need to borrow $20.

00:36.202 --> 00:38.136
- What, dude?
- Just give me some money, man.

00:38.204 --> 00:40.229
- How come you don't ever have any money?
- Dee? Moneys?

00:40.306 --> 00:42.740
- No way.
- What are you gonna do at the strip club with...

00:42.809 --> 00:44.936
- Will you just get in the car!
- No, no!

00:45.011 --> 00:47.809
It sucks for me, 'cause you guys
get all the girls and the attention!

00:47.881 --> 00:50.475
My dad's gonna be here in a second!
Will you get in the car!

00:50.550 --> 00:52.484
- No! I'm going home! I'm going home.
- Oh!

00:52.552 --> 00:55.919
- Can we go? Please!
- Yeah, we can go. We can go.

00:58.091 --> 01:00.150
- Dennis!
- Oh, Jesus!

01:00.226 --> 01:04.026
Dennis, no!

01:04.097 --> 01:06.156
Dennis, you son of a bitch!

01:38.098 --> 01:40.032
What the hell is wrong with you, Dad?

01:40.100 --> 01:42.534
Why would you come sneaking around
the bar in the middle of the night?

01:42.602 --> 01:45.230
You don't snoop and sneak and appear
in front of cars and start yelling names!

01:45.305 --> 01:48.138
- No!
- I had something very important to tell you.

01:48.208 --> 01:50.267
Really? What could be so important
it couldn't wait till the morning?

01:50.343 --> 01:53.608
There's nothing more important than the
fact that we just hit our friend with a car.

01:53.680 --> 01:57.582
Oh, yeah? Try this on for size.
Your mother's dead.

01:57.650 --> 01:59.777
- No.
- What?

01:59.853 --> 02:02.219
Oh, my God!

02:02.288 --> 02:06.987
No, she's not dead.
We're gettin' divorced though.

02:08.495 --> 02:09.519
- Why...
- Why...

02:09.596 --> 02:11.063
- What...
- What...

02:11.131 --> 02:13.565
- Why would you say that she's dead?
- That's a business tactic.

02:13.633 --> 02:17.091
You drop the bomb, then you soften
the blow. You never tried this?

02:18.605 --> 02:22.006
- That is a terrible business tactic!
- You are a horrible father.

02:22.075 --> 02:24.100
That's what I came
to talk to you about.

02:24.177 --> 02:27.943
I hate the kind of person that
your whore mother turned me into.

02:28.014 --> 02:30.915
The big house, the big car...
I'm giving it all away.

02:30.984 --> 02:33.452
- Hmm?
- Giving it away how?

02:33.520 --> 02:37.616
For starters, I'm giving all my money to charity.
Then I'm gonna hang out with you two.

02:37.690 --> 02:39.885
That's what this is all about...
spending time with my kids.

02:39.959 --> 02:42.587
- Hold on a second.
- I wanna be the father that I never was.

02:42.662 --> 02:44.596
- Shh, shh, shh, shh, shh.
- Getting to know them.

02:44.664 --> 02:46.529
- What did you say about the money?
- Mm-hmm.

02:46.599 --> 02:50.057
- I'm giving it all away.
- That is a very stupid thing to do.

02:50.136 --> 02:52.764
You're a very stupid, stupid man.
Who are you gonna give it to?

02:52.839 --> 02:55.330
I don't know.
Poor people.

02:55.408 --> 02:57.603
- Poor people?
- Poor people?

02:57.677 --> 02:59.702
What... What is your prob...
Okay, where's Mom?

02:59.779 --> 03:03.977
Mom? She's on vacation banging
one of the boys she hangs out with.

03:04.050 --> 03:08.510
- Dennis, your mother is a dirty, dirty whore.
- Oh, goddamn it, Dad!

03:08.588 --> 03:10.579
First you force me
to run over my friend Charlie.

03:10.657 --> 03:12.648
And then you start talking
about Mom like she's dead.

03:12.725 --> 03:14.659
- Now you're saying she's a dirty whore?
- The money.

03:14.727 --> 03:17.093
- You can't waltz back into our lives and be our dad again!
- And the money.

03:17.163 --> 03:19.654
- It doesn't work that way. You can't just barge in!
- And the money!

03:19.732 --> 03:23.532
And the money!
My God, Dad! All of our money?

03:32.946 --> 03:35.278
Well, that was awkward.

03:35.348 --> 03:38.476
- Yes, it was.
- Sort of a private conversation.

03:38.551 --> 03:41.520
- Very much a family type moment.
- We didn't need to hear any of that.

03:41.588 --> 03:44.022
Not for our ears.

03:44.090 --> 03:46.923
Wanna go to the strip club?

03:46.993 --> 03:49.188
I don't know.

03:49.262 --> 03:53.494
I've been manically depressed
for the past couple of years.

03:53.566 --> 03:57.662
I just feel like I need a serious change,
or I'm gonna kill myself.

03:57.737 --> 04:00.331
So when you say you're giving
your money away to poor people...

04:00.406 --> 04:03.569
do you mean, like, "Mexico" poor,
or can it be, like, "me and Charlie" poor?

04:05.912 --> 04:08.574
- Well, I haven't given that much thought.
- Put some thought into that one.

04:08.648 --> 04:10.582
- Consider that.
- Yeah, man. Give that some thought.

04:10.650 --> 04:13.744
In the meantime, you wanna
get shit-faced, bro. So I tell you what.

04:13.820 --> 04:16.118
Before we get crazy
giving away our money here...

04:16.189 --> 04:18.248
what do you say we buy
a couple of pitchers...

04:18.324 --> 04:21.691
maybe a few tequila shots,
a few rounds of kamikazes.

04:21.761 --> 04:24.889
After that, we'll hit the town, we'll
tie on a serious buzz. All right, bud?

04:24.964 --> 04:28.229
Oh, my God!
You poor baby. What happened?

04:28.301 --> 04:32.260
Uh, my best friend
ran me over with his car.

04:32.338 --> 04:34.272
Yeah.

04:34.340 --> 04:37.002
- Oh, my God! That's terrible!
- Yeah, yeah.

04:37.076 --> 04:39.636
- Do you want a lap dance?
- Oh...

04:39.712 --> 04:43.148
- I don't have any money.
- Oh!

04:43.216 --> 04:45.150
I could give you one for free.

04:45.218 --> 04:48.119
Really? Okay.
Okay.

04:48.187 --> 04:51.054
Oh, my God! You poor baby.
What happened to you?

04:51.124 --> 04:54.582
- His friend ran him over with a car.
- That is so sad.

04:54.661 --> 04:56.891
I know.
I was gonna give him a free lap dance.

04:56.963 --> 04:58.897
- She totally was.
- I'll join you!

04:58.965 --> 05:02.401
That's great! Do one of you girls
wanna hook my boy up over here?

05:02.468 --> 05:05.369
- He's really down in the dumps.
- Okay!

05:05.438 --> 05:07.633
- No, no, no. I don't... I don't...
- Oh, come on, buddy!

05:07.707 --> 05:09.971
- You gotta do this, man!
- Embrace it. Get in the spirit.

05:10.043 --> 05:11.977
This is gonna cheer you up.

05:16.149 --> 05:19.915
Well, maybe just one.

05:19.986 --> 05:23.820
All right, Frank! See?
That's the spirit that beat theJapanese!

05:25.024 --> 05:27.424
God. Stupid Dad!
Never gave me a goddamn thing.

05:27.493 --> 05:30.985
Give his shit to poor people. Poor people?

05:38.371 --> 05:40.305
Ooh! Ooh!

05:40.373 --> 05:42.170
Oh! Oh.

05:42.241 --> 05:45.472
Dee, you scared the shit out of me.
What are you doing?

05:45.545 --> 05:49.106
Same thing you're doing, Dennis. I'm not
letting Dad give all this shit to poor people.

05:49.182 --> 05:51.673
I got here first though. I'm taking
the plasma TV and the fish tank.

05:51.751 --> 05:54.151
- How come you get to pick and choose?
- It's not that.

05:54.220 --> 05:56.518
I'm a man and I'm strong.
I can carry heavy things.

05:56.589 --> 05:59.524
You're a woman.
You're weak, and you can't.

05:59.592 --> 06:02.493
- You're a woman and you're weak.
- That doesn't make any sense.

06:02.562 --> 06:04.689
- You don't make any sense.
- Great. I'll tell you what.

06:04.764 --> 06:08.291
Um, I'm gonna take all the stuff that
I want and load it into my enormous S. U. V...

06:08.368 --> 06:11.997
and you can grab some trinkets or whatever
and throw it in your tiny little car.

06:12.071 --> 06:15.006
All right, look.
We don't need to be doing this, okay?

06:15.074 --> 06:17.736
You're my brother. We're...
We're in this thing together.

06:17.810 --> 06:19.744
We don't need to make this
a competition.

06:19.812 --> 06:21.746
Yeah.

06:21.814 --> 06:26.478
You're right. A competition.
That's a good idea. I'll make you a deal.

06:26.552 --> 06:29.180
Whatever your feeble little arms
can carry out of here, you can keep.

06:29.255 --> 06:32.247
And the rest is mine.

06:32.325 --> 06:35.419
God, I hate you so bad!

06:35.495 --> 06:38.487
- Okay, you ready?
- Yeah!

06:38.564 --> 06:42.022
On your mark!
Get set! Go!

06:43.936 --> 06:45.870
- Go, go, go!
- Go, horsey!

06:45.938 --> 06:47.838
Come on!
Come on!

06:56.282 --> 06:59.080
No! Wait a second!
Charlie, you hit me!

06:59.152 --> 07:01.017
- You hit me, Charlie!
- So what? So what?

07:01.087 --> 07:03.385
- You are fast.
- I was winning anyway.

07:03.456 --> 07:05.390
This one's too heavy!
This one's too heavy!

07:05.458 --> 07:07.619
- You are freakishly fast!
- Thanks.

07:09.996 --> 07:12.055
Charlie, you got any booze in here?

07:12.131 --> 07:15.532
Yeah, yeah. Check under my bed
or under one of my pillows.

07:15.601 --> 07:17.967
Hey, guys, I can't thank you enough.

07:18.037 --> 07:20.699
I feel so much better.
So much.

07:20.773 --> 07:23.674
Yeah, man. Hey, you look great.
Make yourself at home.

07:23.743 --> 07:26.007
- Charlie, we gotta get him out of here.
- What? Why, dude?

07:26.078 --> 07:28.012
Because there's two of them
and three of us!

07:28.080 --> 07:30.014
Have a heart.
The guy's going through a divorce.

07:30.082 --> 07:32.016
- Since when do you give a shit about people?
- Well, you know.

07:32.084 --> 07:33.642
Maybe you should be
the one that leaves, okay?

07:33.719 --> 07:35.653
Don't you roll away
when I'm talking to you.

07:35.721 --> 07:37.746
- I am the reason the girls are here in the first place.
- That is bullshit!

07:37.824 --> 07:41.419
- Do not ruin this! Do not ruin this for me!
- I'm not ruining anything!

07:41.494 --> 07:44.292
Whoa!
What are you guys fighting about?

07:44.363 --> 07:46.593
Nothing, man.
We're just having a...

07:46.666 --> 07:49.829
Well, take it out in the hall.
You're ruining the vibe.

07:49.902 --> 07:53.235
- Okay. We'll go out in the hall. Watch my... Watch my...
- Shut up!

07:53.306 --> 07:56.503
Easy. Easy!
Your behavior is unbelievable, man.

07:56.576 --> 07:58.544
- All right. How are we gonna do this?
- Okay.

07:58.611 --> 08:02.342
- Uh, let's flip a coin. The loser leaves.
- Great.

08:02.415 --> 08:04.440
- Okay, get a coin.
- I don't have a coin.

08:04.517 --> 08:06.712
- Why don't you...
- Give me a coin. You have a coin?

08:06.786 --> 08:08.686
- Of course I don't have a coin.
- All right.

08:08.754 --> 08:10.688
- Let's flip something else.
- All right. Um...

08:10.756 --> 08:13.384
- Something in the hallway, like a feather.
- Flip that, uh, piece of wood?

08:13.459 --> 08:15.518
- That's not gonna work.
- What about something off the chair?

08:15.595 --> 08:17.529
Yeah. Maybe we'll just
break something off the chair.

08:17.597 --> 08:20.122
Break something... Don't...
Don't break it too much.

08:20.199 --> 08:22.030
- No, that's not gonna work.
- It's a rental, dude.

08:22.101 --> 08:25.468
- You know what? Frank's got money. Let's ask him.
- All right.

08:25.538 --> 08:28.598
- It's locked.
- No. You gotta push it hard 'cause it sticks.

08:28.674 --> 08:31.040
- I'm telling you, it's locked.
- Bang again!

08:31.110 --> 08:33.135
- Frank!
- Frank, open the door, dude!

08:33.212 --> 08:35.146
- Hey.
- Oh.

08:35.214 --> 08:37.444
You guys need to give me about
45 minutes in here, okay?

08:37.517 --> 08:39.451
Here.
Hey, Charlie, here's five dollars.

08:39.519 --> 08:41.783
Go down to Wawa,
pick me up a couple of sodas.

08:41.854 --> 08:44.288
I got a feeling I'll be
pretty thirsty after this.

08:44.357 --> 08:45.949
Yeah. Hey...

08:46.025 --> 08:48.425
Oh...

08:48.494 --> 08:52.331
Son of a bitch.

08:56.034 --> 08:57.968
Over the line.
Over the line!

08:58.036 --> 09:02.302
- I'm... I'm on the line.
- On the line is over the line. Get your foot on your side.

09:02.374 --> 09:04.103
Which side? This one?
Is this the side?

09:04.176 --> 09:05.768
- No.
- This the side you're talking about?

09:05.844 --> 09:08.711
Get... All right. You know what?
Oh, what is this?

09:08.780 --> 09:10.714
Do you recognize this lamp?

09:10.782 --> 09:13.250
- Where'd you get that?
- I think this is the lamp Dad got you in China.

09:13.318 --> 09:15.252
- Give it back to me.
- As I recall, yeah.

09:15.320 --> 09:17.254
- Give me my lamp back.
- Must have gotten this out of your room.

09:17.322 --> 09:19.620
- Well, it's mine.
- Let me put it on your side for you.

09:20.959 --> 09:24.224
- You s...
- Oh, that is a shame.

09:24.296 --> 09:26.230
- No, that's fine. I don't care.
- It slipped.

09:26.298 --> 09:28.766
Yeah. By the way,
I wanted to show you something...

09:28.834 --> 09:30.802
my feeble little arms
were able to carry.

09:30.869 --> 09:33.394
By all means.

09:34.473 --> 09:36.703
- Mr. Tibbs.
- Oh, is that it?

09:36.775 --> 09:40.302
Is that Mr. Tib... Is that what they call you?
They call you Mr. Tibbs?

09:40.379 --> 09:43.974
- What do they call you now?
- Whatever.

09:44.049 --> 09:48.042
I don't care.

09:48.120 --> 09:50.645
Hey-o!

09:50.722 --> 09:52.656
What's up, bitches?

09:52.724 --> 09:56.023
- What?
- Dennis, you would not believe how great this thing is.

09:56.094 --> 10:00.053
People give you free shit, and women treat you
like a puppy they found out on the street.

10:00.132 --> 10:02.066
- Really?
- Yeah. Dude, I was thinking.

10:02.134 --> 10:04.625
You pick up one of these bad boys,
we head down to the mall.

10:04.703 --> 10:07.570
There's a ton of talent down there.
We've been looking for a new angle.

10:07.639 --> 10:10.733
- That does sound like fun.
- Yeah. Yeah, that'll work.

10:10.809 --> 10:14.438
Oh, I'm sorry, Dee. We're putting ourselves
into the shoes of the unfortunate...

10:14.513 --> 10:16.538
see what their world's like,
maybe gain a little perspective.

10:16.615 --> 10:20.051
- What do you do?
- I don't take advantage of people.

10:20.118 --> 10:25.021
- Oh!
- Look at Sweet Dee sitting on her cloud of judgment...

10:25.090 --> 10:28.025
handing down life lessons
to all the sinners.

10:28.093 --> 10:31.392
Come on, Mac.
Let's go get crippled.

10:36.201 --> 10:38.135
Charlie.

10:38.203 --> 10:41.001
- Charlie, buddy, buddy, buddy. Charlie.
- Oh, my God, I'm cold.

10:41.072 --> 10:46.032
- We gotta talk, Charlie.
- Uh... Oh, yeah, Frank. We have to talk.

10:46.111 --> 10:48.579
Last night was one of
the greatest nights of my whole life.

10:48.647 --> 10:52.378
- I'm sure it was.
- I used to live like this in squalor and filth...

10:52.451 --> 10:55.545
always trying to get over on people,
scamming my way through situations.

10:55.620 --> 10:59.056
- Wow! I don't care!
- I wanna live like you again, Charlie.

10:59.124 --> 11:02.890
I wanna be pathetic and desperate
and ugly and hopeless.

11:02.961 --> 11:05.293
- I am not ugly.
- This is the change I've been looking for.

11:05.363 --> 11:07.297
- I wanna move in with you.
- Are you out...

11:07.365 --> 11:10.596
Are you out of your damn mind, dude?
You made me sleep out in the hall.

11:10.669 --> 11:13.103
You ignored my cries for help
in the middle of the night.

11:13.171 --> 11:15.901
- I'll pay for your rent for six months.
- Twelve.

11:15.974 --> 11:16.668
- Six.
- Ten.

11:16.741 --> 11:17.400
- Six.
- Nine.

11:17.476 --> 11:18.170
- Six.
- Ten.

11:18.243 --> 11:19.175
- Six.
- Twelve.

11:19.244 --> 11:20.006
- Four.
- Six.

11:20.078 --> 11:22.012
- Deal.
- All right.

11:22.080 --> 11:24.071
- No more sleeping out in the hall though.
- I can't promise that.

11:24.149 --> 11:25.980
- Let's get ready.
- All right. Where are you taking me?

11:26.051 --> 11:28.281
- We're going back to the strip club.
- All right. Strip club...

11:28.353 --> 11:30.787
- Dude! My legs!
- Hold on a second.

11:30.856 --> 11:33.450
This is going to be like
shooting fish in a barrel for us.

11:33.525 --> 11:35.993
It's gonna be awesome.
What's your backstory?

11:36.061 --> 11:39.724
- What do you mean?
- Bro, your backstory. How'd your legs get crippled?

11:39.798 --> 11:42.494
- I don't know.
- All right, check mine out. I had polio. Okay?

11:42.567 --> 11:44.967
That's why I'm rocking the F. D. R. Look
with the blanket and everything.

11:45.036 --> 11:48.665
See, I got a problem.
My legs are really muscular and athletic.

11:48.740 --> 11:50.901
So nobody's gonna believe
that they're dead. Okay?

11:50.976 --> 11:53.171
This way, with the blanket,
everyone will assume that underneath...

11:53.245 --> 11:55.179
my legs are withered and useless.

11:55.247 --> 11:58.307
- Huh. That's a good idea.
- Bro, it's brilliant.

11:58.383 --> 12:00.317
Yeah.
I have polio too.

12:00.385 --> 12:03.013
You can't have polio. That's my disease.
You gotta pick your own disease.

12:03.088 --> 12:05.716
- Yeah, but I want polio.
- Well, you can't have it.

12:05.790 --> 12:07.724
What the hell is this?

12:09.528 --> 12:11.462
Are you sure you're okay?

12:11.530 --> 12:14.522
It's really important
that I do this myself.

12:14.599 --> 12:17.796
You are so brave.

12:25.277 --> 12:28.542
I got it!
All by myself, I did it.

12:28.613 --> 12:31.081
Yeah, you did.
That's awesome.

12:36.321 --> 12:38.255
Goddamn it.

12:38.323 --> 12:41.417
What are we gonna do now? We can't
go back in there. Everybody's desensitized.

12:41.493 --> 12:43.518
All right, look.
We'll go down to Crate and Barrel.

12:43.595 --> 12:46.655
- Maybe we can find some cougars or something.
- Hey, guys!

12:46.731 --> 12:49.393
Shit! What do we do?
What do we do?

12:49.467 --> 12:51.492
- Uh, okay. Just play it cool, man.
- Play it cool.

12:51.570 --> 12:54.038
Play it cool.

12:54.105 --> 12:55.367
- Hey.
- Hey.

12:55.440 --> 12:57.305
- How's it going?
- I have polio.

12:57.375 --> 12:59.104
Oh.

13:00.478 --> 13:04.346
Uh... Okay.

13:06.051 --> 13:10.647
- And I have polio...
- He has polio too.

13:14.292 --> 13:17.420
Mm-hmm.

13:17.495 --> 13:20.362
All right.
Um...

13:36.047 --> 13:39.380
- So if you wanna shower, you gotta shower in the bar.
- Shower in the bar?

13:39.451 --> 13:41.385
- Yeah. Shower in the sink.
- In the sink?

13:41.453 --> 13:44.820
Yeah. You never showered in a sink bef...
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh...

13:44.889 --> 13:46.823
- What?
- Oh, my God!

13:46.891 --> 13:48.722
- Do you see that?
- What?

13:48.793 --> 13:52.957
I got a good idea. I think I know how we
can really up our game at the strip club.

13:53.031 --> 13:54.965
How?

13:55.033 --> 13:59.402
Who gets more respect and admiration
in this country than war heroes?

13:59.471 --> 14:01.632
- Athletes.
- Yeah, that's true.

14:01.706 --> 14:03.640
- But after that.
- Rock stars.

14:03.708 --> 14:05.835
- Yeah, also true. But after that, Frank.
- Actors.

14:05.910 --> 14:07.502
- Yeah... Right.
- Models.

14:07.579 --> 14:09.012
- Yes. Look...
- Rich people.

14:09.080 --> 14:11.310
Okay, look, look, look!
If you just buy me this costume...

